            This song is one of my favourites and surprisingly easy,
it is three chords throughout, I've only listed the chords
as I'm not good with solos etc.
It is based on C, D and G, although D/F# is sometimes used:
 e   0[C]       [D]2         [D/F#]2           [G]3
 B   1       3         3           0
 G   0       2         2           0
 D   2       0         0           0
 A   3       -         -           2
 E   -       -         2           3

The whole song is four strums on C, then 2 on D, and 2 on G, for a better
effect alternate between strumming and picking notes.

